    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **11 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the change so that a created (and subsequently fetched) owner returns a `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` property (readOnly string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field in responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes `displayName` as `lastName + \", \" + firstName` from the stored entity names (null-safe).\n\nThe controller already returns `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` for both create (`POST /api/owners`) and read (`GET /api/owners/{id}`), so the derived field flows through both paths without further changes. The new `Cp05Tests.coreComputesDisplayName` passes, and all 11 existing tests remain green.",
